In the afternoon, I stepped out of Lonavala's main market.
There was a lot of crowd and chaos in the market.
I wanted some peace.
I started going towards a famous viewpoint.
This road was going up the hill.
The road was very winding.
I was walking slowly.
A man was walking ahead of me.
His water bottle was in his hand.
My own backpack was on my back.
I felt a little thirsty.
I took out my own bottle and drank water.
In Mumbai, there is always a lot of rush.
But here everything was very quiet.
There were big and green trees along the side of the road.
I was walking at my own pace.
The weather was nice and cool.
I went ahead slowly, looking at the nature around me.
